Rust implementations of image models for the CPU and for Vulkan GPUs,
provided under MIT (LICENSE). Each model's crate credits its model and
carries the licence of its weights in its own NOTICE: crates/birefnet-native,
crates/scunet-native, crates/realesrgan-native and crates/lama-native. The
CPU engine they share, crates/native-engine, and their Vulkan shaders build
on the work below.

1. XNNPACK (BSD-3-Clause), by Facebook, Inc. and its affiliates and Google
   LLC. The exponential under the softmax and the sigmoid computes as
   XNNPACK's f32 "p5" kernels do for finite values: the same constants and
   argument reduction, written anew in Rust. The left operand of every matrix
   product is read through row pointers, as XNNPACK's indirect convolution
   reads it. https://github.com/google/XNNPACK
   XNNPACK's licence follows as notice A.

2. Eigen: the error function under the GELU, on the CPU and in the shaders,
   evaluates the 13/8-degree rational fit of generic_fast_erf_float in Eigen
   3.4 (unsupported/Eigen/src/SpecialFunctions/SpecialFunctionsImpl.h, by
   Eugene Brevdo). Only its twelve coefficients and the [-4, 4] clamp are
   taken; no Eigen source is copied. https://gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen


A. XNNPACK, https://github.com/google/XNNPACK

